We have:

\begin{align*}
(1 \bmod 7) &= 1 \\
(3 \bmod 7) &= 3 \\
(5 \bmod 7) &= 5 \\
&\vdots \\
(195 \bmod 7) &= 3 \\
(197 \bmod 7) &= 2 \\
(199 \bmod 7) &= 4
\end{align*}

So the sum of these numbers modulo $7$ is:

\begin{align*}
